From 19f01d55f93ffbe36d80e4dcf7538c3148e16a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snarayana <snarayana@student.ethz.ch>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:42:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: report JIT output the engine leaves outside the
 kept caches

A fixed list of cache variables rots silently: when sglang 0.5.20 moved
load_jit's cache, nothing failed, launches just got ~17 s slower at TP4.
jit_audit snapshots the engine's default cache locations ($HOME's .cache,
.triton, .nv and .tilelang, and the temp dir) before it starts and, once it
is ready, reports every new file outside the kept caches, grouped by
directory, with its size and the variable that moves it, or a note that
servekit knows none:

  [SERVEKIT] warning: the engine compiled into directories servekit does not keep:
  [SERVEKIT]      6.0 kB in     3 files  ~/.cache/sglang/jit  (servekit set SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR, and the engine wrote to its default anyway)

In the temp dir, which also holds runtime scratch, only known caches and
compiled code count; downloads (huggingface, pip, ...) never do. The launch
report's jit_cache section adds the drift and what the run compiled into the
node-local caches, so a partial hit shows. prepare and --only-prepare audit
their warmup run too, after the engine has stopped.

--jit-cache-strict turns drift into exit code 3. prepare still writes its
manifest and caches; a launch stops its server by returning True from
on_ready, which run_profile now honors by terminating the engine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
